<title>UK: Toronto-Dominion Bank sets $200 mln bond.</title>
<headline>Toronto-Dominion Bank sets $200 mln bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Paribas Capital Markets.</p>
<p> BORROWER   TORONTO-DOMINION BANK</p>
<p> AMT    $200 MLN	COUPON     6.50	MATURITY    27.MAR.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.275   PAY DATE    27.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.375     REOFFER    100.10    SPREAD	+14 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AA2	 LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA	  DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/CA</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ONTARIO   HOME CTRY  CANADA    TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.20	SELL CONC  1.175     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 5.875 PCT FEBRUARY 2000 GOVERNMENT BOND</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p> NOTES	TORONTO-DOMINION AND UBS ARE JOINT LEAD MANAGERS</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
